course: dictionary
lesson: 1954
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Compact» can describe something small, something pressed tightly, a small case, or an agreement. The words around it tell you which meaning to use. «From a stile they look back at the wood, "dense, menacing, compact"» means the trees are packed closely together, not that the wood is small.
explain: Look for clues in the sentence. «"Compact" in a house advert means small, and "deceptively spacious" usually means small too.» The advert is for a home, so compact means small. Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Compare the meaning with the words around it. «Air pushes back on falling things, and it slows light, fluffy or flat things far more than heavy, compact ones.» Light and fluffy is the opposite of compact here, so compact means small and solid, packed together tightly.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Compact» means small and neatly packed, so it does not take up much space.
fact: «Compact» can also mean a small flat case with a mirror and face powder, or a formal agreement between people or countries.
fact: To compact something is to press it together tightly so it takes less space.
fact: Compact soil or snow is pressed tightly together.
exercise: «The house was compact, with one small kitchen and two bedrooms.» What does compact mean here? | Loud and busy | Very old and falling down | *Small and neatly packed | Wet and muddy
exercise: Mia opened her «compact» to check her face in the tiny mirror. What is a compact here? | *A small flat case with a mirror and face powder | A large box for toys | A kind of bus ticket | A type of soil
exercise: Two countries signed a «compact» to share the river fairly. What is a compact here? | A tiny car | A small flat case | A pile of pressed snow | *An agreement between people or countries
test: «The snow on the path was compact and hard, so the sledge slid well.» What does compact mean? | *Pressed tightly together | Hidden under leaves | Melting quickly | Light and fluffy
test: The workers used a machine to «compact» the rubbish before it went to the tip. What does compact mean here? | To paint in bright colours | To wash thoroughly | To pour out slowly | *To press together tightly so it takes less space
exam: What does «compact» mean in «a compact camera that fits in a pocket»? | Made of stone | Very expensive | *Small enough to carry easily | Hard to use
